title: croak leaks module paths and line numbers into user-facing error messages
updated: 2026-08-10T14:57:44Z
---

Carp appends the call site even when the message ends in a newline, so
user-facing errors leak module paths:

    cd /tmp/not-a-repo && karr list
    Not a git repository. karr requires Git.
     at /storage/raid/home/getty/dev/perl/p5-app-karr/lib/App/karr/Role/BoardDiscovery.pm line 124.

(`perl -MCarp -e 'eval { croak "msg\n" }; print $@'` confirms Carp ignores the
trailing-newline convention that `die` honours.)

Affected: `Role/BoardDiscovery.pm:119` and both sync failures in
`Role/SyncLifecycle.pm`, so **every** remote failure ends with
`at .../Cmd/Create.pm line 116.`. Meanwhile `die "Task N not found\n"` is clean,
so the CLI's error style is inconsistent depending on which code path you hit.

Related noise on the same path: a failing pull prints the identical multi-line
git error four times (once per attempt plus the final croak), and `--quiet`
suppresses the "Pull retry 2 of 3" lines but not the repeated error bodies.

Fix: `die` for user-facing messages, keep `croak` for programming errors; print
the underlying git error once.
Partially done. The mechanism exists: lib/App/karr/Error.pm with user_error
(plain die, honours the trailing newline Carp ignores) and clean_error (strips
"at FILE line N." plus trailing backend lines, reads ->message on libgit2-style
objects). App::karr::Git::_ref_write_error should fold into clean_error — the
->message branch was written so that fold is a pure deletion.

Applied only in Cmd/List.pm and Cmd/Skill.pm; the rest was under concurrent edit.
